# Local artifacts that must never reach the public mirror.
#
# This file exists because the mirror is copied with `rsync --delete` /
# `robocopy /MIR`, which is a FILESYSTEM mirror: it copies whatever is sitting
# in the staged directory, tracked or not. Without a .gitignore in the PUBLIC
# repo, a `git add -A` after that copy stages local junk and publishes it.
#
# On 2026-08-05 the sibling tree (release/strixgov-skills/) had no .gitignore
# of its own, so `/MIR` PURGED the public repo's copy — and the very same push
# then published a locally-generated Ed25519 demo key from `demo/.solo/`, which
# that purged file had been ignoring. The file must live HERE, in staging, or
# the next mirror deletes it again.
#
# scripts/verify-public-push-safety.mjs additionally refuses to push when the
# staged tree contains files untracked in this monorepo — belt and braces, since
# ignoring a file is not the same as noticing it.

# Local Mode /strix-wire key material + run state (never publishable)
.solo/

# Dependency + build output
node_modules/

# Python bytecode / test caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# OS + editor noise
.DS_Store
*.log
